In silico PCR (sPCR) and incremental kmer counting from whole-genome shotgun reads

Usage: sharkmer [OPTIONS] [INPUT]...

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Input:
  [INPUT]...       FASTQ input files (.fastq or .fastq.gz). Reads from stdin if omitted
      --ena <ENA>  Stream reads directly from ENA by accession (e.g. SRR5324768)

Output:
  -s, --sample <SAMPLE>  Sample name (output file prefix; required unless --ena derives it)
  -o, --outdir <OUTDIR>  Output directory [default: ./]

PCR:
      --pcr-panel <PCR_PANEL>            Use a preconfigured primer panel (repeatable)
      --pcr-panel-file <PCR_PANEL_FILE>  Load a primer panel from a YAML file or URL (repeatable)
      --pcr-primers <PCR_PRIMERS>        Specify a primer pair inline (repeatable, see --help-pcr)
      --no-emit-uncertain                Exclude sequences with assembly warnings from FASTA output

PCR info:
      --list-panels                  List available primer panels and exit
      --export-panel <EXPORT_PANEL>  Export a built-in panel as YAML to stdout and exit
      --help-pcr                     Show detailed help for --pcr-primers format
      --dump-graph                   Write assembly graphs as annotated DOT (Graphviz) files
      --validate-panels              Validate primer panels/primers and exit

Kmer:
  -k <K>  Kmer length [default: 19]

Incremental counting:
      --chunks <CHUNKS>        Number of incremental chunks (0 = skip histograms) [default: 0]
      --histo-max <HISTO_MAX>  Maximum histogram count value [default: 10000]

General:
  -t, --threads <THREADS>
          Number of threads [default: 1]
  -m, --max-reads <MAX_READS>
          Maximum number of reads to process (default: all)
      --min-kmer-count <MIN_KMER_COUNT>
          Minimum kmer count for sPCR (filters low-count kmers before PCR) [default: 2]
      --validate-every <VALIDATE_EVERY>
          Validate FASTQ format every N records (0 = first record only) [default: 0]
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace)
  -q, --quiet
          Suppress all output except errors
      --color <COLOR>
          Color output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --cite
          Print citation information and exit
      --completions <SHELL>
          Print shell tab-completion script and exit [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]
      --dry-run
          Validate inputs and print what would happen, then exit

Cache:
      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>  Override cache directory for remote reads
      --no-cache               Disable read caching (stream directly, do not read from or write to cache)
      --clear-cache            Delete the read cache directory and exit

Example:
  Extract cnidarian genes from ENA reads (downloads automatically):
  sharkmer --ena SRR23143286 --pcr-panel cnidaria -m 1000000 -o output

Output files:
  {outdir}/{sample}.stats.yaml             Run statistics (always produced)

  PCR:
  {outdir}/{sample}_{gene}.fasta           sPCR products per gene

  Incremental counting (--chunks > 0):
  {outdir}/{sample}.histo                  All incremental histograms
  {outdir}/{sample}.final.histo            Final histogram
sharkmer 3.2.0 (https://github.com/caseywdunn/sharkmer)
Available PCR panels (use --export-panel <name> for details):

  angiospermae     v2.0.0    Universal plant primers for chloroplast and ITS products (10 primers)
  bacteria         v1.0.0    Bacterial 16S metabarcoding primers (6 primers)
  c_elegans        v1.0.2    Development panel for Caenorhabditis elegans (N2 strain). Exact primers (no degeneracy) for mitochondrial, ribosomal, and single-copy nuclear genes. Designed for benchmarking sPCR recovery of nuclear SCGs. (8 primers)
  cnidaria         v1.1.2    Universal and custom primers targeting mitochondrial and nuclear products. (7 primers)
  human            v1.0.2    Human mitochondrial primers from Ramos et al. 2009. doi: 10.1002/elps.200800601 (9 primers)
  hydrozoa         v1.0.9    Primers targeting mitochondrial and nuclear markers for Hydrozoa (Cnidaria: Hydrozoa), covering hydroids, siphonophores, leptothecates, and trachylines. (4 primers)
  insecta          v1.0.2    Multiple primer sets, including universal and Drosophila specific, as well as for broad metazoan markers (21 primers)
  metazoa          v1.0.0    Metazoa 18S metabarcoding primers (7 primers)
  teleostei        v1.0.2    Universal fish primers for mitochondrial and nuclear products (5 primers)
sharkmer 3.2.0

If you use sharkmer in published work, please cite:

For in silico PCR:

  Dunn and Church (2026) Sharkmer: repurposing PCR primers for
  targeted genome assembly using in silico PCR.
  Bioinformatics, btag163.
  doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btag163

